Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:01:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gx: zero spot coefficients ignore an unset light direction

A point light that sets only a0 of its angle attenuation (GXInitLightAttn
with a1 = a2 = 0, GX_AF_SPOT) may leave its direction uninitialised, as
TTYD's map lights do (a GXLightObj on the stack). On hardware a zero
coefficient contributes nothing; here 0 * NaN, or 0 * inf when the
garbage's square overflowed, made the light's attenuation NaN and lit
nothing, so walls lit only by such lights went black depending on what the
stack held (TTYD's Excess Express corridor). A zero coefficient now adds 0.
---
--- a/lib/gx/shader.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/shader.cpp
@@ -805,7 +805,11 @@ auto lighting_func(const ShaderConfig& config, const ColorChannelConfig& cc, u8
   } else if (cc.attnFn == GX_AF_SPOT) {
     lightAttnFn = fmt::format(R"""(
           var cosine = max(0.0, dot(ldir, light.dir));
-          var cos_attn = dot(light.cos_att, vec3f(1.0, cosine, cosine * cosine));
+          // A zero coefficient contributes nothing, as on hardware: a light that only sets
+          // a0 (a point light) may leave its direction unset, and 0 * NaN or 0 * inf from
+          // that garbage would otherwise turn the light black.
+          var cos_attn = light.cos_att.x + select(0.0, light.cos_att.y * cosine, light.cos_att.y != 0.0) +
+                         select(0.0, light.cos_att.z * cosine * cosine, light.cos_att.z != 0.0);
           var dist_attn = dot(light.dist_att, vec3f(1.0, dist, dist2));
           attn = max(0.0, cos_attn / dist_attn);)""");
   } else if (cc.attnFn == GX_AF_SPEC) {
